id: pm-xrjy8o
title: "GH-1136: npm 12 object-form npm pack receipts break registry package installs"
description: "Track GitHub issue #1136: npm 12 changed `npm pack --json` from an array to an object keyed by package name. The package-source parser accepts only the older array shape and then misclassifies valid but unrecognized JSON as a line-oriented filename, producing a tar path ending in `}` and breaking every explicit npm extension install."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,github,npm,package-ecosystem,regression
created_at: "2026-08-28T14:42:31.427Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:44:40.120Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Parse npm 11 array and npm 12 object receipts through one typed SDK-owned contract; select the requested entry deterministically; never apply a filename fallback after JSON parsed successfully; add npm 11/12 unit, integration, packed-consumer, and negative malformed-shape coverage; preserve actionable structured CLI errors."
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1136
severity: high
environment: "npm 12.0.2, Node 26.5.0, Linux; explicit npm: package sources"
repro_steps: "Run `pm package install npm:pm-brief` under npm 12.0.2; observe the valid object-form pack receipt fall through to a tarball path named `}`."
expected_result: "The package source accepts every documented npm pack JSON shape, selects the requested package deterministically, and fails closed with a shape-specific diagnostic when well-formed JSON is unsupported."
actual_result: "Object-form npm 12 receipts are ignored after successful JSON parsing; the last pretty-printed line `}` is treated as a filename and tar fails with ENOENT."
affected_version: 2026.8.27-2026.8.28
component: package-install
regression: true
customer_impact: "All explicit registry extension installs are broken for users on current npm 12, including every published first-party package."
